WEBVTT

00:00:16.327 --> 00:00:18.728
♪ ♪

00:00:31.342 --> 00:00:33.743
♪ ♪

00:00:47.824 --> 00:00:50.026
♪ ♪

00:00:58.835 --> 00:01:01.037
♪ ♪

00:01:07.244 --> 00:01:09.280
♪ ♪

00:01:10.581 --> 00:01:12.383
Ever since we...

00:01:15.184 --> 00:01:17.987
You're the only person that I've ever...

00:01:18.821 --> 00:01:21.392
Sorry, this is weird. I-I don't talk like this.

00:01:21.425 --> 00:01:23.126
WOMAN: No, it's okay.

00:01:28.064 --> 00:01:32.168
I feel like I'm coming apart.

00:01:34.338 --> 00:01:37.974
I think about you all the time, Nikki.

00:01:39.643 --> 00:01:41.811
I try not to...

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.815
...you're in every song I listen to.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.918
You were the only person who was nice to me

00:01:48.951 --> 00:01:50.387
When I moved here.

00:01:50.421 --> 00:01:53.089
And at first, I thought maybe you...

00:01:58.094 --> 00:02:01.864
Well, I realized who you are.

00:02:02.965 --> 00:02:06.936
And then, after Nana passed, you were the one that called

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:09.340
Even when I didn't have anything to say

00:02:09.373 --> 00:02:11.074
And we just sat there.

00:02:12.942 --> 00:02:14.611
So I keep telling myself, "Don't tell her.

00:02:14.645 --> 00:02:16.012
"She's too good.

00:02:16.045 --> 00:02:19.082
And she'll... you'll lose her."

00:02:20.517 --> 00:02:23.420
But maybe you should know...

00:02:25.054 --> 00:02:27.123
...that I would choose you over everything.

00:02:28.925 --> 00:02:30.193
Aw. (chuckles)

00:02:30.227 --> 00:02:31.662
-That's everything. -IAN: No, no. Stop.

00:02:31.695 --> 00:02:34.231
-Okay, th-th-that was cringey. -Oh, my God. I knew it.

00:02:34.264 --> 00:02:35.366
-IAN: Way too much. -I-I'm so sorry.

00:02:35.399 --> 00:02:37.066
WOMAN: I thought that was sweet.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.435
-I thought it was gross. -BEAR: I-I should've...

00:02:38.469 --> 00:02:39.636
-Okay, this time I want you... -BEAR: No, I...

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:41.137
I'm not doing it again, dude.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:42.506
-That was so embarrassing. -IAN: Yeah, yeah.

00:02:42.539 --> 00:02:44.073
That would freak... Th-Th-That freaked me out.

00:02:44.107 --> 00:02:45.376
Okay? Nikki would vomit.

00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:46.976
You told me to pour my heart out.

00:02:47.009 --> 00:02:48.144
Do you know how vulnerable I just got?

00:02:49.011 --> 00:02:50.381
I underestimated you.

00:02:50.414 --> 00:02:52.148
-What if you got her something nice? -IAN: No, no.

00:02:52.181 --> 00:02:53.484
-I'll try that. -IAN: D-Don't get her anything.

00:02:53.517 --> 00:02:54.618
(stammers) Dude, you got to be less...

00:02:54.651 --> 00:02:57.019
Way less sappy with Nikki, okay?

00:02:57.053 --> 00:02:58.422
She doesn't like that shit. She doesn't.

00:02:58.455 --> 00:03:01.991
Flowers, the candy that she said she likes?

00:03:02.024 --> 00:03:03.460
IAN: Okay.

00:03:03.494 --> 00:03:05.027
Thank you.

00:03:05.061 --> 00:03:06.497
WOMAN: What?

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:07.564
Thank you.

00:03:07.598 --> 00:03:09.299
WOMAN: You want me to go?

00:03:09.333 --> 00:03:11.000
-Yeah, if-if you want, yeah. -WOMAN: Oh, yeah, okay. Yeah.

00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:12.569
I'm sorry that... I'm sorry I made you do that.

00:03:12.603 --> 00:03:14.003
No. No, it's okay. You're okay.

00:03:14.036 --> 00:03:15.272
-No, it-it just... -It's a fun break.

00:03:15.305 --> 00:03:16.673
-Just pretend like... -You're good.

00:03:16.707 --> 00:03:20.377
(chuckles) Oh, my God, dude, that was so embarrassing.

00:03:20.411 --> 00:03:21.645
Can we leave?

00:03:21.678 --> 00:03:24.415
Yeah, well, thank God I did it. That was... that was awful.

00:03:24.448 --> 00:03:26.149
Thank you for that.

00:03:26.182 --> 00:03:28.918
Have you ever actually, like, flirted with Nikki?

00:03:29.553 --> 00:03:31.053
Invite romance.

00:03:31.722 --> 00:03:34.391
-Invite romance? -Tease her.

00:03:34.425 --> 00:03:36.560
-Be playfully mean with her. -Be mean to her?

00:03:36.593 --> 00:03:39.229
Playfully mean, yeah, but bring up Freaky Nikki.

00:03:39.263 --> 00:03:40.997
You want me to call her Freaky Nikki?

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.399
You know she's sensitive about that.

00:03:42.433 --> 00:03:43.966
Be like, "Hey, remember when you used to get bullied?

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.035
Everybody called you Freaky Nikki?"

00:03:46.068 --> 00:03:47.438
She'll be like, "Oh, my God.

00:03:47.471 --> 00:03:49.606
"Oh, no, Bear, that was... that was so long ago.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.308
Don't. Please."

00:03:51.909 --> 00:03:54.611
And that will, like, take her breath away?

00:03:54.645 --> 00:03:57.180
Just say,

00:03:57.214 --> 00:04:00.082
"Nikki, I think we should grab a drink sometime."

00:04:00.116 --> 00:04:01.218
Yeah, I've grabbed drinks sometimes.

00:04:01.251 --> 00:04:02.586
She always invites you.

00:04:02.619 --> 00:04:04.086
-Yeah, exactly. -I asked you guys not to come

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:05.522
To trivia for one night.

00:04:05.556 --> 00:04:07.291
Y-You can't ask her out at trivia, Bear.

00:04:07.324 --> 00:04:08.991
You can't. I-I'm not gonna let you.

00:04:09.025 --> 00:04:10.627
It's a good, organic time to ask.

00:04:10.661 --> 00:04:12.329
I love trivia night.

00:04:12.362 --> 00:04:13.263
It's all I have.

00:04:13.297 --> 00:04:15.198
I wake up every Wednesday

00:04:15.232 --> 00:04:16.567
Rock hard, thinking about trivia.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:19.068
God, I can't get over how dumb I just looked.

00:04:19.101 --> 00:04:20.437
Y-You can't turn our weekly gathering

00:04:20.471 --> 00:04:22.272
Of camaraderie and skill i-into your... your...

00:04:22.306 --> 00:04:24.241
Your seven-year-late promposal, Bear.

00:04:24.274 --> 00:04:26.477
Then when do I ask?

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.512
Any other time.

00:04:28.545 --> 00:04:30.481
All you have is time.

00:04:30.514 --> 00:04:33.217
♪ ♪

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.219
If she means this much to you--

00:04:35.252 --> 00:04:38.755
And I know she does-- wait.

00:04:38.789 --> 00:04:40.524
Do it at the right time.

00:04:41.758 --> 00:04:43.427
Okay.

00:04:45.462 --> 00:04:46.330
Okay, I'll wait.

00:04:46.363 --> 00:04:48.565
-I'll do it right. -Now say it with me.

00:04:49.633 --> 00:04:52.269
All you have is time.

00:04:52.302 --> 00:04:55.339
-(indistinct chatter on TV) -(door creaking)

00:04:57.808 --> 00:04:59.376
BEAR: Oh, no.

00:05:00.544 --> 00:05:02.212
Sandy?

00:05:04.113 --> 00:05:05.282
Sandy?

00:05:05.315 --> 00:05:07.618
(Bear breathing heavily)

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:12.222
(quietly): Oh, no.

00:05:13.423 --> 00:05:15.292
(voice shaking): Sandy?

00:05:16.627 --> 00:05:18.262
No.

00:05:18.295 --> 00:05:20.264
No, no, no, no.

00:05:21.298 --> 00:05:23.667
(sobbing): Oh, no, no. No, no!

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.068
Oh, shit.

00:05:27.237 --> 00:05:29.606
How did you get into these?

00:05:31.608 --> 00:05:33.510
Oh, man.

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:52.462
(Bear sobbing)

00:06:03.607 --> 00:06:05.509
Why can't she...

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:08.378
Just...

00:06:11.915 --> 00:06:14.318
♪ ♪

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.655
(clock ticking)

00:06:25.796 --> 00:06:28.130
(phone vibrating)

00:06:33.303 --> 00:06:35.305
-Hey. -NIKKI: Wow, you are so lucky.

00:06:35.339 --> 00:06:37.608
Today was so busy.

00:06:37.641 --> 00:06:38.875
(chuckles): Oh.

00:06:38.909 --> 00:06:40.544
I needed a good day off.

00:06:40.577 --> 00:06:42.346
Oh, yeah. Definitely. (chuckles)

00:06:42.379 --> 00:06:45.616
-You work so hard. -(laughs)

00:06:45.649 --> 00:06:46.617
You know I do.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:48.485
Oh, uh, what time are you showing up tonight?

00:06:48.518 --> 00:06:50.654
I want to secure the spot early.

00:06:50.687 --> 00:06:52.356
Oh.

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:55.325
Um, I'll...

00:06:57.628 --> 00:07:00.931
I don't think I'm gonna make it tonight, actually.

00:07:00.964 --> 00:07:02.799
Aw, Bear, no.

00:07:02.833 --> 00:07:04.368
I wanted to see you tonight.

00:07:04.401 --> 00:07:05.636
We need your brain.

00:07:05.669 --> 00:07:07.270
We got to beat the Rag Tags this week.

00:07:07.304 --> 00:07:09.506
Uh, well, I mean...

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:12.209
I...

00:07:13.142 --> 00:07:14.911
I-I don't... I don't think I can tonight.

00:07:14.945 --> 00:07:17.514
I'm just catching up on some stuff.

00:07:19.416 --> 00:07:22.452
I was gonna tell you something.

00:07:22.486 --> 00:07:23.720
What?

00:07:23.754 --> 00:07:25.656
I mean, should I, like, tell you now?

00:07:25.689 --> 00:07:27.290
Yeah.

00:07:27.924 --> 00:07:29.559
What?

00:07:32.562 --> 00:07:36.333
Yeah, so I'm putting in my two weeks.

00:07:38.502 --> 00:07:39.736
Really?

00:07:43.974 --> 00:07:45.575
How come?

00:07:47.844 --> 00:07:49.780
I don't know.

00:07:49.813 --> 00:07:53.817
Yeah, we're kind of running out of time, Bear, so, um...

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:56.219
You know, might want to skip that stuff

00:07:56.253 --> 00:07:57.988
You're working on. (chuckles)

00:07:58.021 --> 00:07:59.956
BEAR: You're right.

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:01.692
-Tonight's the night. -Shit!

00:08:01.725 --> 00:08:02.893
Goddamn it!

00:08:02.926 --> 00:08:04.528
Are you okay?

00:08:04.561 --> 00:08:06.963
No, I just dropped my crystal necklace down the drain.

00:08:06.997 --> 00:08:09.566
-Oh, shit. -Ugh!

00:08:09.599 --> 00:08:11.234
Sorry.

00:08:13.503 --> 00:08:15.405
-Why would she even say that? -(bell chimes, door opens)

00:08:15.439 --> 00:08:16.640
Hey, uh, we're closing soon,

00:08:16.673 --> 00:08:18.408
So let me know if you need anything.

00:08:18.442 --> 00:08:19.609
-BEAR: Oh, o-okay. -(indistinct chatter on phone)

00:08:19.643 --> 00:08:21.344
-Thank you. -Right. Yeah, I know.

00:08:21.378 --> 00:08:22.846
Ryan was saying that, too, so I'm not the only one.

00:08:22.879 --> 00:08:24.448
MAN (on phone): Oh, you're definitely not the only one.

00:08:24.481 --> 00:08:26.016
-I know. -BEAR: Hey, uh, sorry.

00:08:26.049 --> 00:08:27.484
I-I do need help.

00:08:27.517 --> 00:08:30.353
Um, do you have, uh, crystal necklaces?

00:08:30.387 --> 00:08:32.422
Yeah. Yeah, here, let me show you.

00:08:32.456 --> 00:08:34.324
No, honestly, 'cause that's what I was saying before.

00:08:34.357 --> 00:08:36.493
Like, what? What are you even talking about?

00:08:40.363 --> 00:08:41.865
Oh, my God, that's crazy.

00:08:41.898 --> 00:08:43.300
-What? -No.

00:08:43.333 --> 00:08:44.468
Hold on a second.

00:08:44.501 --> 00:08:45.869
Um, so this is all we have.

00:08:45.902 --> 00:08:47.738
Yeah, each rock has its own

00:08:47.771 --> 00:08:50.474
Kind of unique energy and whatever.

00:08:50.507 --> 00:08:52.509
So, the amethyst is for calmness, clarity,

00:08:52.542 --> 00:08:55.045
And then the rose quartz attracts, like, love and shit.

00:08:55.078 --> 00:08:58.915
What's one that's, like, good...

00:08:58.949 --> 00:09:01.384
Energy or, like, good vibes?

00:09:01.418 --> 00:09:03.386
Probably the citrine.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:06.623
I mean, it's basically sunshine in a rock.

00:09:06.656 --> 00:09:08.391
Okay. Thanks.

00:09:08.425 --> 00:09:10.694
Yeah. Let me know if you need anything else.

00:09:11.528 --> 00:09:12.996
Sunshine in a rock.

00:09:13.029 --> 00:09:14.498
Well, no, 'cause yesterday at lunch,

00:09:14.531 --> 00:09:16.433
Becca was being, like, such a... Yeah.

00:09:16.466 --> 00:09:18.468
Nikki would hate that.

00:09:19.569 --> 00:09:21.638
No, that's what I'm saying.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.509
And then her bringing Ryan with her?

00:09:25.542 --> 00:09:27.811
I was like, "What are you even doing?"

00:09:27.844 --> 00:09:29.880
♪ ♪

00:09:32.082 --> 00:09:33.316
Like, really?

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:35.253
You know we don't even like him.

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:38.588
Just so annoying.

00:09:40.757 --> 00:09:42.325
Yeah.

00:09:44.694 --> 00:09:46.830
Honestly, 'cause that's what I was saying...

00:09:46.863 --> 00:09:48.732
(chatter fades)

00:09:59.476 --> 00:10:01.845
What, no crystal?

00:10:01.878 --> 00:10:03.647
I like this.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:06.516
Yeah, well, they've been pretty popular since we put them out.

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:08.618
You know, everybody wants a wish.

00:10:11.655 --> 00:10:14.090
Well, it's not for me, so...

00:10:14.124 --> 00:10:17.427
Okay, well, don't come back complaining. (chuckles)

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:18.895
Do people complain about these or...?

00:10:18.929 --> 00:10:20.897
Well, they're kind of like collectibles,

00:10:20.931 --> 00:10:23.633
So some people don't open them, but the people who do,

00:10:23.667 --> 00:10:26.336
You know, come back and complain.

00:10:29.873 --> 00:10:31.575
'Cause it's a scam or...?

00:10:31.608 --> 00:10:33.577
Hey, man, we're not scammers, okay?

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:34.845
No, no, I don't mean that you're a scammer,

00:10:34.878 --> 00:10:36.947
But just, like, why do they complain?

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:39.716
'Cause they're mad

00:10:39.749 --> 00:10:41.651
-'cause it doesn't work? -Yeah, or whatever.

00:10:41.685 --> 00:10:45.455
(laughing): Or it does work and it, like, ruins their lives?

00:10:45.488 --> 00:10:47.023
Or they die or wish they were dead.

00:10:47.057 --> 00:10:49.459
(Bear laughs)

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:51.795
You're good, very good.

00:10:51.828 --> 00:10:53.663
Yeah, you could write a review.

00:10:53.697 --> 00:10:55.599
-This is gonna be seven... -(buttons clicking)

00:10:55.632 --> 00:10:57.968
NIKKI: Have you ever even been into a Guitar Center?

00:10:58.001 --> 00:10:59.636
-SARAH: No. -NIKKI: They aren't all tuned.

00:10:59.669 --> 00:11:01.037
-So, basically... -It's not about the guitars,

00:11:01.071 --> 00:11:02.839
-and you know that. -Those teenagers are fucking

00:11:02.873 --> 00:11:04.608
Slapping it like a bass, and the shitty demo strings--

00:11:04.641 --> 00:11:05.976
-don't even get me started. -IAN: Ladies, please.

00:11:06.009 --> 00:11:07.677
He doesn't expect them to be tuned all the time.

00:11:07.711 --> 00:11:09.012
-It's... -(Ian groans)

00:11:09.045 --> 00:11:10.647
If you're working on your book or whatever...

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:12.048
-IAN: Girls. -...or you're on the clock,

00:11:12.082 --> 00:11:13.750
-it would give you something to do. -Oh, my God.

00:11:13.783 --> 00:11:15.151
I never work on my book when there are customers

00:11:15.185 --> 00:11:16.786
In the store, so why does it matter?

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.555
I know, but look, I'm the one that has to go home

00:11:18.588 --> 00:11:21.491
And hear my dad complain about my friends all night.

00:11:21.524 --> 00:11:22.826
I'm just asking you to pretend

00:11:22.859 --> 00:11:24.761
-like you're working. -IAN (whispers): What?

00:11:24.794 --> 00:11:26.162
-Just, like... -NIKKI: I mean, it's easy

00:11:26.196 --> 00:11:27.631
-for you to say... -No.

00:11:27.664 --> 00:11:29.099
...when you're leaving for tattoo school.

00:11:29.132 --> 00:11:31.768
SARAH: It's art school, and I haven't gotten in yet.

00:11:31.801 --> 00:11:33.204
I thought you got into Luther.

00:11:33.237 --> 00:11:34.871
SARAH: No, I said I want to go to Luther.

00:11:34.905 --> 00:11:36.773
-NIKKI: Sorry, I didn't... -SARAH: Still have a shot.

00:11:36.806 --> 00:11:38.141
-NIKKI: Good. -SARAH: Sorry. -(whispers): Later.

00:11:38.174 --> 00:11:39.976
-I-I just don't want you to get in trouble. -Later.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:41.544
-NIKKI: I know, babe. I love you. -SARAH: I love you.

00:11:41.578 --> 00:11:43.480
What the fuck are you guys doing?

00:11:43.513 --> 00:11:45.615
-IAN: Uh... -Ian's just messing with me.

00:11:45.649 --> 00:11:47.984
I look over, and these two are just... (mouthing)

00:11:48.018 --> 00:11:49.085
(laughter)

00:11:49.119 --> 00:11:50.887
IAN: Hey, cut the shit.

00:11:50.921 --> 00:11:52.989
Hey, can we focus up? This is, uh, this is very serious to me.

00:11:53.023 --> 00:11:54.591
I'm gonna go get some shots.

00:11:54.624 --> 00:11:55.725
-SARAH: Great idea, Nikki. -I'll-I'll come with you.

00:11:55.759 --> 00:11:57.160
NIKKI: Thank you. Thank you.

00:11:57.193 --> 00:11:59.230
SARAH (laughs): What the fuck were you guys doing?

00:11:59.263 --> 00:12:00.664
(whispers): After.

00:12:00.697 --> 00:12:02.499
NIKKI: Four shots of tequila, please.

00:12:02.532 --> 00:12:03.967
Um, and anything else?

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.669
I'll get a piña colada.

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:08.672
A piña colada?

00:12:08.705 --> 00:12:10.740
-Don't make fun of my drink. -(Nikki laughing)

00:12:10.774 --> 00:12:12.075
-What? -(laughing): I like a man

00:12:12.108 --> 00:12:14.945
Who's in touch with his feminine side.

00:12:14.978 --> 00:12:16.546
-Why is that feminine? -It's not.

00:12:16.579 --> 00:12:17.814
I don't like the taste of the alcohol.

00:12:17.847 --> 00:12:20.750
-Yeah, we'll get you juice. -Wow.

00:12:21.385 --> 00:12:22.919
Wait, so what was the important stuff

00:12:22.953 --> 00:12:24.988
-on the phone today? -A lot.

00:12:25.021 --> 00:12:26.656
I did a lot of really important things.

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:28.692
-That? -Cleaned.

00:12:28.725 --> 00:12:31.494
-Mm. -I did my taxes.

00:12:31.528 --> 00:12:33.663
-I did... -You watched TV all day.

00:12:33.697 --> 00:12:35.865
-Yeah, that's all I did. -(both laugh)

00:12:35.899 --> 00:12:37.268
Bear.

00:12:37.301 --> 00:12:38.902
Yeah.

00:12:41.004 --> 00:12:42.806
So, uh, I was thinking...

00:12:42.839 --> 00:12:44.241
BARTENDER: Got a card for the shots?

00:12:44.275 --> 00:12:45.842
NIKKI: Uh, yes.

00:12:45.875 --> 00:12:46.943
I got it.

00:12:46.977 --> 00:12:48.511
Okay, fine. Yes.

00:12:48.545 --> 00:12:50.847
You can... But I think...

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:52.549
-Ah. -I said I got it.

